  <h2 id="short-answer">The short answer to "is DevOps a good career"</h2>

  <p>
    DevOps is a real, growing field in India, not a hype cycle waiting to pop. But "is DevOps good" and "will I
    personally get a well-paid DevOps job easily" are two different questions, and most articles on this topic blur
    them together until you cannot tell which one is actually being answered.
  </p>

  <p>
    The honest split is this: DevOps, SRE, and platform-engineering hiring at product companies and Global
    Capability Centres is growing faster than general IT hiring and paying strongly for engineers who can prove
    real infrastructure skill. DevOps work at IT-services firms carries the same job title but noticeably lower pay
    and slower progression, because the work often stays closer to ticket-driven operations than infrastructure
    ownership. Neither tier is fake — they are just genuinely different markets wearing the same job title.
  </p>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      This is not the "DevOps is the hottest tech career, get certified in 90 days" pitch flooding course ads, and
      it is not an AI-panic warning that the role is disappearing either. Both miss the real picture. The field
      genuinely pays well and is genuinely growing, and it genuinely carries an on-call, incident-response weight
      that most course marketing quietly leaves off the brochure. Both things are true at once.
    </p>
  </div>

