  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--amber">
    <p>
      A counter-intuitive but consistent signal in current industry reporting: AI adoption itself is adding to
      DevOps demand, not shrinking it, because every company deploying AI systems needs someone to build and operate
      the infrastructure those systems run on. Tools like GitHub Copilot speed up writing a Terraform module or a
      CI/CD config from a known pattern, but they do not design the architecture, decide the trade-off, or own the
      incident when something breaks in production at 2am. That judgment layer keeps paying well; the risk sits
      mostly with engineers doing pure routine execution with no proof of judgment behind it.
    </p>
  </div>

